      "standardized_narrative": "At 1 January 2021 the syndicate's gross claims outstanding were GBP 794.858m. Analysis of the gross claims development triangle shows adverse prior-year development on the 2019 underwriting year of approximately GBP 14.9m (c.1.9% of opening reserves), indicating a net strengthening of reserves for pre-2020 years. Overall syndicate liabilities fell materially during 2021 largely due to the RITC transfer of 2018 and prior years to an external party which reduced gross claims outstanding by c.GBP 511.5m. Reported influences during the year include COVID-19 effects from 2020, named losses such as Hurricane Ida and civil unrest in South Africa, and the review of provisions following the FCA Business Interruption Test Case which did not require material additional provisioning.",
